# X-Plane Web API

- Base: `http://localhost:8086/api/v3` and `ws://localhost:8086/api/v3`
- Pin `/api/v3` as a constant for future bumps
- Capabilities: read/write DataRefs, activate Commands, subscribe (~10 Hz)
- Docs: https://developer.x-plane.com/article/x-plane-web-api/

## Invariants

- DataRef and Command **numeric IDs are session-scoped** — resolve again after every X-Plane restart
- API is localhost-only (Stream Deck and X-Plane on same machine)

## Debug

Before blaming the plugin, smoke the API:

```bash
curl 'http://localhost:8086/api/v3/datarefs?filter[name]=sim/cockpit2/controls/gear_handle_down'
```

Script: `scripts/smoke-client.ts`. Logs after install: `~/Library/Logs/ElgatoStreamDeck/`

